      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "German immigrant farmers arrived in the early 19th century, and mid‑century coal mining drove the town’s growth into the early 1900s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Fairview_Heights,_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The construction of Interstate 64 in the 1960s connected Fairview Heights directly to St. Louis, sparking a wave of commercial expansion.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Fairview_Heights,_Illinois",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Abandoned underground mines left a legacy of subsidence risks that still affect modern infrastructure in Fairview Heights.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Fairview_Heights,_Illinois",
